IMPORT prelude

-- Legislation Act 2003 (Commonwealth): the definitions in sections 4, 5 and 6 and the meaning of "legislative instrument"
-- and "notifiable instrument" in sections 8 to 11, so far as the text of sections 12 to 54 uses them.
-- Text: C2004A01224.txt, compilation C2019C00084; it is not the authorised text.
--
-- A definition that says "means" answers JUST FALSE for a case it does not name; one that says "includes" or lists
-- without closing the list answers NOTHING.
-- Terms that the Dictionary only points at ("see section 15J") are encoded where the text defines them.

§ `Section 4: the Dictionary (terms with a meaning stated in the Dictionary itself)`

-- src:75 | commencement instrument, in relation to an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, means an instrument providing solely for the commencement of:
-- src:76 | (a) the Act or instrument; or
-- src:77 | (b) a provision of the Act or instrument.
-- src:78 | Example: A Proclamation providing solely for the commencement of an Act.
@ref s 4 "commencement instrument" (src:75-78)
GIVEN `it provides for the commencement of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for the commencement of a provision of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides for anything else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the instrument is a commencement instrument` MEANS
    JUST (   (`it provides for the commencement of the Act or instrument` OR `it provides for the commencement of a provision of the Act or instrument`)
         AND NOT `it provides for anything else`)

-- src:79 | compilation, of an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, is a document showing the text of the Act or instrument:
-- src:80 | (a) as amended (if at all) and in force on a day (the compilation date) stated in the document; or
-- src:81 | (b) as the Act or instrument would be amended and in force on a day (the compilation date) stated in the document, by amendments that have not commenced, if the document indicates that the amendments have not commenced; or
-- src:82 | (c) as the Act or instrument is, or would be, modified by an Act or an instrument, and in force on a day (the compilation date) stated in the document.
-- src:83 | Note: See Part 2 of Chapter 2 for the registration of compilations.
@ref s 4 "compilation" (src:79-83)
GIVEN `it shows the text as amended (if at all) and in force on a compilation date stated in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it shows the text as it would be amended by amendments that have not commenced, and indicates that they have not commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it shows the text as modified by an Act or an instrument, and in force on a compilation date stated in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the document is a compilation` MEANS
    JUST (   `it shows the text as amended (if at all) and in force on a compilation date stated in the document`
          OR `it shows the text as it would be amended by amendments that have not commenced, and indicates that they have not commenced`
          OR `it shows the text as modified by an Act or an instrument, and in force on a compilation date stated in the document`)

-- src:106 | primary law means an Act or an instrument made under an Act, or a provision of an Act or an instrument made under an Act.
@ref s 4 "primary law" (src:106-106)
GIVEN `it is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a provision of an Act or of an instrument made under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the law is a primary law` MEANS
    JUST (`it is an Act` OR `it is an instrument made under an Act` OR `it is a provision of an Act or of an instrument made under an Act`)

-- src:89 | enabling legislation, in relation to a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, means the primary law that authorises the making of the instrument.
@ref s 4 "enabling legislation" (src:89-89)
GIVEN `the law is a primary law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law authorises the making of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the law is the enabling legislation for the instrument` MEANS
    JUST (`the law is a primary law` AND `the law authorises the making of the instrument`)

-- src:94 | instrument means any writing or other document, and includes an instrument in electronic form.
@ref s 4 "instrument" (src:94-94)
GIVEN `it is a writing or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the thing is an instrument` MEANS
    JUST (`it is a writing or other document` OR `it is in electronic form`)

-- src:97 | making, in relation to an instrument, means the signing, sealing or other endorsement of the instrument by the person or body empowered to make it.
@ref s 4 "making" (src:97-97)
GIVEN `it is the signing, sealing or other endorsement of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is done by the person or body empowered to make the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the act is the making of the instrument` MEANS
    JUST (`it is the signing, sealing or other endorsement of the instrument` AND `it is done by the person or body empowered to make the instrument`)

-- "includes": the cases the text names answer JUST TRUE; any other case is not covered.
DECLARE `Way of ending a provision` IS ONE OF
    repeal
    revoke
    rescind
    omit

-- src:109 | repeal, in relation to an instrument or a provision of an instrument, includes revoke or rescind the instrument or provision.
-- src:110 | Note: Section 5 defines amend, for a provision of an instrument, to include the repeal of a provision of the instrument.
@ref s 4 "repeal" (src:109-110)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of ending a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the way of ending a provision is a repeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN repeal THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN revoke THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN rescind THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN omit THEN NOTHING

-- src:102 | power delegated by the Parliament: an instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament includes:
-- src:103 | (a) an instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament to a person or body and then, under the authority of the Parliament, further delegated by that person or body to another person or body; and
-- src:104 | (b) an instrument that may be made under a power delegated by the Parliament as well as under a power given otherwise by law.
-- src:105 | Example: An instrument made under an Act as well as a prerogative power.
@ref s 4 "power delegated by the Parliament" (src:102-105)
GIVEN `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament to a person or body and then, under the authority of the Parliament, further delegated to another` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be made under a power delegated by the Parliament as well as under a power given otherwise by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the instrument is made under a power delegated by the Parliament` MEANS
    IF `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament to a person or body and then, under the authority of the Parliament, further delegated to another`
       OR `it may be made under a power delegated by the Parliament as well as under a power given otherwise by law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:118 | text includes any writing.
-- src:119 | Note: See the definition of writing in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.
@ref s 4 "text" (src:118-119)
GIVEN `it is writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the thing is text` MEANS
    IF `it is writing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Defined by reference to another Act: the borrowed fact is an input.
-- src:92 | First Parliamentary Counsel means the person appointed to the position of First Parliamentary Counsel under subsection 4(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970.
@ref s 4 "First Parliamentary Counsel" (src:92-92)
GIVEN `the person was appointed to the position of First Parliamentary Counsel under subsection 4(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the person is the First Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    JUST `the person was appointed to the position of First Parliamentary Counsel under subsection 4(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970`

-- src:101 | Office of Parliamentary Counsel means the office established by subsection 2(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970.
@ref s 4 "Office of Parliamentary Counsel" (src:101-101)
GIVEN `the office was established by subsection 2(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the office is the Office of Parliamentary Counsel` MEANS
    JUST `the office was established by subsection 2(1) of the Parliamentary Counsel Act 1970`

-- src:91 | Federal Register of Legislation means the register established and maintained under section 15A.
@ref s 4 "Federal Register of Legislation" (src:91-91)
GIVEN `it is the register established and maintained under section 15A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the register is the Federal Register of Legislation` MEANS
    JUST `it is the register established and maintained under section 15A`

-- src:107 | register means register on the Federal Register of Legislation.
@ref s 4 "register" (src:107-107)
GIVEN `it is registration on the Federal Register of Legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: to register is to register on the Federal Register of Legislation` MEANS
    JUST `it is registration on the Federal Register of Legislation`

-- Section 61A is outside the scope of this encoding (Chapter 4); whether the rules were made under it is a borrowed fact.
-- src:115 | rules means rules made by the First Parliamentary Counsel under section 61A.
-- src:116 | Note: These rules are legislative instruments. Regulations may also be made for the purposes of this Act (see section 62).
@ref s 4 "rules" (src:115-116)
GIVEN `they are rules made by the First Parliamentary Counsel under section 61A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4: the instrument is the rules` MEANS
    JUST `they are rules made by the First Parliamentary Counsel under section 61A`

§ `Section 5: amend and modify`

DECLARE `Change to an Act, an instrument or a provision` IS ONE OF
    `repeal or omit it, or a part of it`
    `substitute another provision for it, or a part of it`
    `insert another provision into it, or a part of it`
    `renumber it, or a part of it`
    `relocate it, or a part of it`
    `amend it by implication`
    `change its text in any other way`
    `a change that leaves its text as it is`

-- src:121 | (1) In this Act, amend includes:
-- src:122 | (a) for an Act or instrument—repeal, omit, insert, substitute, renumber or relocate a provision of the Act or instrument; and
-- src:123 | (b) for a provision of an Act or instrument—any of the following:
-- src:124 | (i) repeal or omit the provision (or a part of it);
-- src:125 | (ii) substitute another provision for the provision (or a part of it);
-- src:126 | (iii) insert another provision into the provision (or a part of it);
-- src:127 | (iv) renumber the provision (or a part of it);
-- src:128 | (v) relocate the provision (or a part of it); and
-- src:129 | (c) for an Act or instrument, or a provision of an Act or instrument—amend by implication; and
-- src:130 | (d) for an Act or instrument, or a provision of an Act or instrument—change its text in any other way.
@ref s 5(1) (src:121-130)
GIVEN `the change` IS A `Change to an Act, an instrument or a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(1): the change is an amendment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `repeal or omit it, or a part of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `substitute another provision for it, or a part of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `insert another provision into it, or a part of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `renumber it, or a part of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `relocate it, or a part of it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `amend it by implication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `change its text in any other way` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a change that leaves its text as it is` THEN NOTHING

-- src:133 | (2) In this Act, modify an Act or instrument means modify the operation of the Act or instrument without amending its text.
@ref s 5(2) (src:133-133)
GIVEN `it modifies the operation of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it amends the text of the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2): the change is a modification` MEANS
    JUST (`it modifies the operation of the Act or instrument` AND NOT `it amends the text of the Act or instrument`)

§ `Section 6: rule-maker and responsible person`

DECLARE `How an instrument is made` IS ONE OF
    `made by the Governor-General under enabling legislation`
    `made by the Governor-General in any other case`
    `made by a person other than the Governor-General`

DECLARE `Rule-maker` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister currently responsible for administering the provision of the enabling legislation under which the instrument is made`
    `the Prime Minister, or a Minister prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 6(1)(b)`
    `a person currently authorised to make the instrument`

-- src:135 | Rule-makers
-- src:136 | (1) In this Act, rule-maker, for an instrument, means:
-- src:137 | (a) for an instrument made by the Governor-General that is made under enabling legislation (whether or not it may also be made under any other power)—the Minister currently responsible for administering the provision of the enabling legislation under which the instrument is made; or
-- src:138 | (b) for an instrument made by the Governor-General, in any other case—the Prime Minister, or a Minister prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph; or
-- src:139 | (c) for an instrument made by a person other than the Governor-General—a person currently authorised to make the instrument.
@ref s 6(1) (src:135-139)
GIVEN `how the instrument is made` IS A `How an instrument is made`
GIVETH A `Rule-maker`
`s 6(1): the rule-maker for the instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the instrument is made`
    WHEN `made by the Governor-General under enabling legislation` THEN `the Minister currently responsible for administering the provision of the enabling legislation under which the instrument is made`
    WHEN `made by the Governor-General in any other case` THEN `the Prime Minister, or a Minister prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 6(1)(b)`
    WHEN `made by a person other than the Governor-General` THEN `a person currently authorised to make the instrument`

DECLARE `Law concerned` IS ONE OF
    `an Act or a provision of an Act`
    `an instrument`

DECLARE `Responsible person` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister currently responsible for administering the Act or provision`
    `the rule-maker for the instrument`

-- src:140 | Responsible persons
-- src:141 | (2) In this Act, responsible person means:
-- src:142 | (a) for an Act or a provision of an Act—the Minister currently responsible for administering the Act or provision; or
-- src:143 | (b) for an instrument—the rule-maker for the instrument.
@ref s 6(2) (src:140-143)
GIVEN `the law concerned` IS A `Law concerned`
GIVETH A `Responsible person`
`s 6(2): the responsible person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the law concerned`
    WHEN `an Act or a provision of an Act` THEN `the Minister currently responsible for administering the Act or provision`
    WHEN `an instrument` THEN `the rule-maker for the instrument`

-- src:144 | (3) If more than one Minister is currently responsible for administering an Act, or a provision of an Act:
-- src:145 | (a) each of those Ministers is a responsible person for the Act or provision (as the case may be); and
-- src:146 | (b) the performance of a function or duty under this Act (in relation to the Act or provision administered) by any of the Ministers discharges the function or duty.
@ref s 6(3) (src:144-146)
GIVEN `the number of Ministers currently responsible for administering the Act or provision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6(3)(a): each of those Ministers is a responsible person` MEANS
    `the number of Ministers currently responsible for administering the Act or provision` GREATER THAN 1

@ref s 6(3)(b) (src:144-146)
GIVEN `the number of Ministers currently responsible for administering the Act or provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those Ministers who performed the function or duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(3)(b): the performance of a function or duty by any of the Ministers discharges it` MEANS
    IF `the number of Ministers currently responsible for administering the Act or provision` GREATER THAN 1
    THEN (IF `the number of those Ministers who performed the function or duty` AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 8: legislative instrument`

DECLARE `Facts about an instrument for section 8` HAS
    `a primary law gives power to do the thing by legislative instrument and the thing is done`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is registered as a legislative instrument`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of it determines the law or alters the content of the law`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a provision of it has the direct or indirect effect of affecting a privilege or interest, imposing an obligation, creating a right, or varying or removing an obligation or right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is declared by section 10 or 57A to be a legislative instrument`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is declared by an Act not to be a legislative instrument`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 8(6)(b)`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a notifiable instrument because of subsection 11(1)`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a commencement instrument`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a compilation of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is rules of court or a compilation of rules of court`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument or for rules of court`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:168 | Primary law provides for something to be done by legislative instrument
-- src:169 | (2) If a primary law gives power to do something by legislative instrument, then:
-- src:170 | (a) if the thing is done, it must be done by instrument; and
-- src:171 | (b) that instrument is a legislative instrument.
@ref s 8(2) (src:168-171)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(2): a primary law provides for the thing to be done by legislative instrument, and it is done` MEANS
    `the facts`'s `a primary law gives power to do the thing by legislative instrument and the thing is done`

-- src:177 | Instruments registered on the Federal Register of Legislation
-- src:178 | (3) An instrument made under a power delegated by the Parliament is a legislative instrument if it is registered as a legislative instrument.
@ref s 8(3) (src:177-178)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(3): the instrument is made under a power delegated by the Parliament and registered as a legislative instrument` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament`
    AND `the facts`'s `it is registered as a legislative instrument`

-- src:181 | (4) An instrument is a legislative instrument if:
-- src:182 | (a) the instrument is made under a power delegated by the Parliament; and
-- src:183 | (b) any provision of the instrument:
-- src:184 | (i) determines the law or alters the content of the law, rather than determining particular cases or particular circumstances in which the law, as set out in an Act or another legislative instrument or provision, is to apply, or is not to apply; and
-- src:185 | (ii) has the direct or indirect effect of affecting a privilege or interest, imposing an obligation, creating a right, or varying or removing an obligation or right.
@ref s 8(4) (src:181-185)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(4): the instrument determines or alters the law and affects rights or obligations` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament`
    AND `the facts`'s `a provision of it determines the law or alters the content of the law`
    AND `the facts`'s `a provision of it has the direct or indirect effect of affecting a privilege or interest, imposing an obligation, creating a right, or varying or removing an obligation or right`

-- src:187 | (5) An instrument is a legislative instrument if it is declared by section 10 or 57A to be a legislative instrument.
@ref s 8(5) (src:187-187)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(5): the instrument is declared by section 10 or 57A to be a legislative instrument` MEANS
    `the facts`'s `it is declared by section 10 or 57A to be a legislative instrument`

-- src:190 | (6) Despite subsections (4) and (5), an instrument is not a legislative instrument if it is:
-- src:191 | (a) declared by an Act not to be a legislative instrument; or
-- src:192 | (b) prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 8(6) (src:190-192)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(6): the instrument is declared or prescribed not to be a legislative instrument` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is declared by an Act not to be a legislative instrument`
    OR  `the facts`'s `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 8(6)(b)`

-- src:193 | (7) However, subsection (6) does not apply to an instrument that is a legislative instrument under subsection (3) by registration.
@ref s 8(7) (src:193-193)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument under subsection (3) by registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(7): subsection (6) applies to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument under subsection (3) by registration` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:194 | (8) Despite anything else in this section, the following are not legislative instruments, and cannot become legislative instruments under subsection (3) (by being registered as legislative instruments):
-- src:195 | (a) an instrument that is a notifiable instrument because of subsection 11(1) (primary law gives power to do something by notifiable instrument);
-- src:196 | (b) a commencement instrument;
-- src:197 | (c) a compilation of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument;
-- src:198 | (d) rules of court or a compilation of rules of court;
-- src:199 | (e) an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument, or rules of court mentioned in paragraph (d).
@ref s 8(8) (src:194-199)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 8(8): the instrument cannot be a legislative instrument` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is a notifiable instrument because of subsection 11(1)`
    OR  `the facts`'s `it is a commencement instrument`
    OR  `the facts`'s `it is a compilation of a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument`
    OR  `the facts`'s `it is rules of court or a compilation of rules of court`
    OR  `the facts`'s `it is an explanatory statement for a legislative instrument or for rules of court`

-- Subsection (8) governs "despite anything else in this section"; subsection (6) governs "despite subsections (4) and (5)" only,
-- and subsection (7) keeps it away from an instrument that is a legislative instrument by registration under subsection (3).
-- src:166 | (1) A legislative instrument is an instrument to which subsection (2), (3), (4) or (5) applies.
-- src:167 | Note: Instruments that can be legislative instruments may be described by their enabling legislation in different ways, for example as regulations, rules, ordinances or determinations.
@ref s 8(1) (src:166-167)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 8`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8: the instrument is a legislative instrument` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `cannot be one` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `by subsection (2)` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `by subsection (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `by subsection (4) or (5)` AND `declared or prescribed not to be one` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `by subsection (4) or (5)` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `cannot be one` MEANS `s 8(8): the instrument cannot be a legislative instrument` `the facts`
        `by subsection (2)` MEANS `s 8(2): a primary law provides for the thing to be done by legislative instrument, and it is done` `the facts`
        `by subsection (3)` MEANS `s 8(3): the instrument is made under a power delegated by the Parliament and registered as a legislative instrument` `the facts`
        `by subsection (4) or (5)` MEANS
            `s 8(4): the instrument determines or alters the law and affects rights or obligations` `the facts`
            OR `s 8(5): the instrument is declared by section 10 or 57A to be a legislative instrument` `the facts`
        `declared or prescribed not to be one` MEANS `s 8(6): the instrument is declared or prescribed not to be a legislative instrument` `the facts`

§ `Section 9: no inference of legislative character`

-- src:202 | No implication of legislative character (or otherwise)
-- src:203 | (1) The fact that an instrument is a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(2), (3) or (5) does not imply that the instrument is, or must be, of legislative character (within the ordinary meaning of that term).
-- src:204 | (2) The fact that an instrument is not a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(6) does not imply that the instrument is not, or must not be, of legislative character (within the ordinary meaning of that term).
@ref s 9(1) and (2) (src:202-204)
GIVEN `it is a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(2), (3) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1): being a legislative instrument under subsection 8(2), (3) or (5) implies that the instrument is of legislative character` MEANS
    IF `it is a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(2), (3) or (5)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 9(2) (src:204-204)
GIVEN `it is not a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2): not being a legislative instrument under subsection 8(6) implies that the instrument is not of legislative character` MEANS
    IF `it is not a legislative instrument because of subsection 8(6)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:205 | No inference for other instruments
-- src:206 | (3) In determining whether an instrument made under a provision of a primary law is a legislative instrument under subsection 8(4), no inference may be drawn from the fact that an instrument made under another provision of that primary law, or any other primary law, is a legislative instrument, or is not a legislative instrument.
@ref s 9(3) (src:205-206)
GIVEN `the question is whether an instrument made under a provision of a primary law is a legislative instrument under subsection 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(3): an inference may be drawn from the status of an instrument made under another provision of the primary law or any other primary law` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether an instrument made under a provision of a primary law is a legislative instrument under subsection 8(4)` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 10: instruments declared to be legislative instruments`

-- src:215 | (2) The following Territory Ordinances are covered by this subsection:
-- src:216 | (a) an Ordinance made under a power delegated by the Parliament in an Act providing for the government of a non-self-governing Territory;
-- src:217 | (b) an Ordinance made under subsection 12(1) of the Seat of Government (Administration) Act 1910 that has not become an enactment (as defined in the Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988).
@ref s 10(2) (src:215-217)
GIVEN `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament in an Act providing for the government of a non-self-governing Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under subsection 12(1) of the Seat of Government (Administration) Act 1910 and has not become an enactment (as defined in the Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2): the Territory Ordinance is covered by this subsection` MEANS
    IF `it is made under a power delegated by the Parliament in an Act providing for the government of a non-self-governing Territory`
       OR `it is made under subsection 12(1) of the Seat of Government (Administration) Act 1910 and has not become an enactment (as defined in the Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:209 | (1) For the purposes of subsection 8(5), each of the following is a legislative instrument:
-- src:210 | (a) a regulation or Proclamation (other than a Proclamation that is a commencement instrument) made under a power delegated by the Parliament;
-- src:211 | (b) a Territory Ordinance covered by subsection (2), or a regulation, rule or by-law under such an Ordinance;
-- src:212 | (c) an instrument prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph;
-- src:213 | (d) an instrument that includes a provision that amends or repeals another legislative instrument.
@ref s 10(1) (src:209-213)
GIVEN `it is a regulation or Proclamation made under a power delegated by the Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Proclamation that is a commencement instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Territory Ordinance covered by subsection (2), or a regulation, rule or by-law under such an Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 10(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes a provision that amends or repeals another legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1): section 10 declares the instrument to be a legislative instrument` MEANS
    IF   (`it is a regulation or Proclamation made under a power delegated by the Parliament` AND NOT `it is a Proclamation that is a commencement instrument`)
      OR `it is a Territory Ordinance covered by subsection (2), or a regulation, rule or by-law under such an Ordinance`
      OR `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 10(1)(c)`
      OR `it includes a provision that amends or repeals another legislative instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 11: notifiable instrument`

DECLARE `Facts about an instrument for section 11` HAS
    `a primary law gives power to do the thing by notifiable instrument and the thing is done` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a commencement instrument for an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or for a provision of one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a legislative instrument`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 11(2)(b)`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is registered as a notifiable instrument and made under a power delegated by the Parliament or another power given by law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it includes a provision that amends or repeals another notifiable instrument`            IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:220 | (1) If a primary law gives power to do something by notifiable instrument, then:
-- src:221 | (a) if the thing is done, it must be done by instrument; and
-- src:222 | (b) that instrument is a notifiable instrument.
@ref s 11(1) (src:220-222)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 11`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(1): a primary law provides for the thing to be done by notifiable instrument, and it is done` MEANS
    `the facts`'s `a primary law gives power to do the thing by notifiable instrument and the thing is done`

-- src:228 | (2) Each of the following is a notifiable instrument:
-- src:229 | (a) a commencement instrument for an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or for a provision of an Act or such an instrument;
-- src:230 | (b) an instrument, other than a legislative instrument, prescribed by regulation for the purposes of this paragraph;
-- src:231 | (c) an instrument, other than a legislative instrument, that is registered as a notifiable instrument, if the instrument is made under a power delegated by the Parliament or another power given by law;
-- src:232 | (d) an instrument, other than a legislative instrument, that includes a provision that amends or repeals another notifiable instrument.
@ref s 11(2) (src:228-232)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 11`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(2): the instrument is one that subsection (2) lists as a notifiable instrument` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `it is a commencement instrument for an Act, legislative instrument or notifiable instrument, or for a provision of one`
    OR (    NOT `the facts`'s `it is a legislative instrument`
        AND (   `the facts`'s `it is prescribed by regulation for the purposes of paragraph 11(2)(b)`
             OR `the facts`'s `it is registered as a notifiable instrument and made under a power delegated by the Parliament or another power given by law`
             OR `the facts`'s `it includes a provision that amends or repeals another notifiable instrument`))

@ref s 11(2) (src:228-232)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts about an instrument for section 11`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11: the instrument is a notifiable instrument` MEANS
    IF `s 11(1): a primary law provides for the thing to be done by notifiable instrument, and it is done` `the facts` OR `s 11(2): the instrument is one that subsection (2) lists as a notifiable instrument` `the facts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:234 | Modification of the operation of this Act
-- src:235 | (3) The enabling legislation for a notifiable instrument, or a regulation under this Act in relation to a notifiable instrument, may modify the operation of this Act in relation to the instrument.
@ref s 11(3) (src:234-235)
GIVEN `it is a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(3): the enabling legislation or a regulation under this Act may modify the operation of this Act in relation to the instrument` MEANS
    IF `it is a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:237 | Registration to satisfy other publication or notification requirements
-- src:238 | (4) If an Act or an instrument requires an instrument (other than a legislative instrument), or the particulars of the instrument’s making, to be published or notified in the Gazette or in any other way, then, unless the contrary intention appears, the requirement is taken to be satisfied if the instrument is registered as a notifiable instrument.
@ref s 11(4) (src:237-238)
GIVEN `an Act or an instrument requires an instrument other than a legislative instrument, or the particulars of its making, to be published or notified in the Gazette or in any other way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is registered as a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(4): the requirement to publish or notify is taken to be satisfied` MEANS
    IF    `an Act or an instrument requires an instrument other than a legislative instrument, or the particulars of its making, to be published or notified in the Gazette or in any other way`
      AND `the instrument is registered as a notifiable instrument`
      AND NOT `the contrary intention appears`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
